  "prefLabel": "Adm 1002.02 Conviction",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Adm 1002.02 \"Conviction\" means a final judgment on a verdict, finding, or plea of guilty against a defendant charged with a crime. The term includes “convicted”. The term also includes a finding of delinquency against a juvenile charged with delinquency.\n\nSource. #13050, eff 7-1-20",
